Ensure cross-device and cross-browser compatibility.
Implement feature flags for controlled rollouts.
Consider internationalization for units and formats (e.g., calories vs. kilojoules).
Verify data sources and calculation formulas for accuracy, especially for health-related features.


4. Issue Resolution

Clarify the issue with detailed information.
Reproduce the issue in a controlled environment.
Analyze front-end, back-end, and database.
Check recent changes for regressions.
Test for compatibility issues across devices and browsers.
Debug systematically.
Propose and implement fixes.
Validate fixes across devices.
Deploy and monitor.
Document issues and resolutions.
Check third-party services if involved.


5. Coding Standards and Best Practices

Use clear, descriptive names for files, variables, and functions.
Write readable, maintainable code with comments for complex parts.
Follow the project’s directory structure.
Use TypeScript unless specified otherwise.
Keep user-facing text simple and jargon-free.
