6. User Experience and Accessibility

Design intuitive interfaces for beginners.
Follow accessibility guidelines (e.g., ARIA, semantic HTML, keyboard navigation).
Test UI for usability and accessibility.
Provide clear feedback for user actions (e.g., success messages, error alerts).
Design responsive layouts for all screen sizes.
Optimize for touch interfaces on mobile devices.
Handle offline scenarios gracefully with user notifications.


7. Security and Data Privacy

Never expose sensitive data in code or logs.
Validate and sanitize all user inputs.
Use best practices for authentication (e.g., NextAuth.js).
Encrypt sensitive data in transit and at rest.
Review security settings regularly.
Use HTTPS for all network requests.
Configure CORS to allow only trusted origins.
Validate and sanitize file uploads (e.g., check file types, sizes).
Protect authentication tokens and user sessions.


8. Testing and Quality Assurance

Write tests for new features and fixes.
Use Jest and React Testing Library for frontend and API tests.
Mock external services in tests.
Run tests before task completion.
Fix failing tests promptly.
Test across devices and browsers regularly.
Validate nutritional data accuracy and calculations.


9. Documentation and Onboarding

Document features, components, and APIs in Markdown.
Update PROJECT_BLUEPRINT.md as the project evolves.
Write onboarding guides for users and contributors.
Maintain a changelog of major updates.
Use JSDoc for code comments.


10. Continuous Improvement and Maintenance

Update rules when new patterns or best practices emerge.
Add examples from the actual codebase.
Remove outdated patterns.
Cross-reference related rules.
Monitor code reviews and development questions for improvement ideas.
Mark deprecated rules and document migration paths.


11. Additional Expert Rules

Version Control: Use Git with meaningful commit messages and feature branches. Push code to GitHub for major changes.
Code Reviews: Implement a review process (self or team) to ensure quality.
Performance Optimization: Profile the app regularly to address bottlenecks (e.g., optimize load times, reduce resource usage).
User Feedback Loop: Enable easy feedback submission and issue reporting.
CI/CD Pipelines: Automate testing and deployment to reduce errors.
Dependency Management: Keep dependencies updated and monitor for vulnerabilities.
Internationalization: Plan for multi-language support and unit conversions.
Backups and Recovery: Implement regular database backups and a recovery plan.
Monitoring and Logging: Track app health and log events (excluding sensitive data).
Scalability: Design architecture to handle increased load.
Asynchronous Handling: Ensure proper error handling for promises and async/await.
